1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,190
Every coin is a fighter.

2
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,296
Mempire is a real-time,

3
00:00:04,316 --> 00:00:07,361
one-versus-one card battler, where Bitcoin,

4
00:00:07,381 --> 00:00:09,845
memecoins and stocks fight in the arena,

5
00:00:09,865 --> 00:00:11,772
and the market decides who is strong

6
00:00:11,792 --> 00:00:12,727
today.

7
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,775
Price moves become small,

8
00:00:14,804 --> 00:00:16,340
bounded buffs and nerfs,

9
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:19,048
written on chain by a Chainlink workflow.

10
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,008
Two players stake, battle for three minutes,

11
00:00:22,028 --> 00:00:23,518
and every card they drop is a

12
00:00:23,538 --> 00:00:25,262
Monad transaction.

13
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:26,769
That only works on a chain this

14
00:00:26,789 --> 00:00:27,477
fast.

15
00:00:27,497 --> 00:00:29,233
So we built it on Monad.

16
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,333
This is the live app on Monad

17
00:00:33,353 --> 00:00:34,230
testnet.

18
00:00:34,584 --> 00:00:36,552
That strip is Monad itself:

19
00:00:36,813 --> 00:00:38,732
each block voted in about three hundred

20
00:00:38,752 --> 00:00:41,692
milliseconds, and final in under six hundred,

21
00:00:41,712 --> 00:00:43,367
measured in this browser.

22
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,265
One tap as a guest.

23
00:00:45,456 --> 00:00:48,060
The relayer mints an eight-card starter deck,

24
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:50,788
sends test AUSD, and a little MON

25
00:00:50,808 --> 00:00:51,673
for gas.

26
00:00:51,702 --> 00:00:53,052
About ten seconds.

27
00:00:53,072 --> 00:00:55,110
No wallet, no faucet.

28
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:58,100
The side boards show the market meta:

29
00:00:58,176 --> 00:01:00,199
who is buffed, who is nerfed,

30
00:01:00,219 --> 00:01:02,001
and how old the snapshot is.

31
00:01:02,355 --> 00:01:04,715
We pick the one-dollar tier in MON,

32
00:01:04,735 --> 00:01:07,435
and both players queue a ranked match.

33
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:13,970
Now every card I drop is its

34
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:16,965
own transaction, signed by a per-match session

35
00:01:16,985 --> 00:01:19,162
key, so there are no popups.

36
00:01:19,516 --> 00:01:21,949
Each pill shows the real round trip:

37
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,178
executed, then final.

38
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,749
When the second player's claim lands,

39
00:01:40,769 --> 00:01:42,563
the contract settles the pot:

40
00:01:42,592 --> 00:01:44,151
ninety percent to the winner,

41
00:01:44,171 --> 00:01:45,698
ten to the house.

42
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:50,259
Empire reads Monad's native staking precompile live,

43
00:01:50,279 --> 00:01:53,068
and checks passkey signatures with the P-256

44
00:01:53,088 --> 00:01:54,116
precompile.

45
00:01:54,679 --> 00:01:57,863
New players can even open chests gaslessly,

46
00:01:57,883 --> 00:02:01,980
through EIP-7702 and our own paymaster.

47
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,803
Clans, and clan wars,

48
00:02:03,823 --> 00:02:05,962
score only the staked wins the relay

49
00:02:05,982 --> 00:02:07,498
has verified on chain.

50
00:02:07,759 --> 00:02:09,643
These clans were seeded by our team

51
00:02:09,663 --> 00:02:10,795
for the demo.

52
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:15,511
Mempire.

53
00:02:15,531 --> 00:02:16,966
Every coin is a fighter.

54
00:02:16,994 --> 00:02:18,878
Play it now, at mempire monad,

55
00:02:18,898 --> 00:02:20,669
dot vercel, dot app.
